{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "11", "m": "09", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "06", "M": "46", "S": "13"}}, "news": [{"title": "Nagpur civic body rules out amnesty to defaulters as tax recovery drive gathers pace", "para": "The Nagpur Municipal Corporation has turned down a proposed property tax amnesty scheme. This decision coincides with their intensified campaign to recover outstanding dues from major defaulters. The standing committee chairperson highlighted the importance of fairness to diligent taxpayers. As part of their strategy, the civic body is now proceeding with property seizures and issuing warnings about possible service disconnections.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/nagpur-civic-body-rules-out-amnesty-to-defaulters-as-tax-recovery-drive-gathers-pace/134050567?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-89326/134050567.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "DDA holds consultations on Delhi master plan 2047 implementation", "para": "The Delhi Development Authority has initiated discussions regarding the implementation of the Master Plan for Delhi 2047. Key focus areas included enhancing inter-departmental collaboration and strategies for transport-oriented development. Additionally, notable conversations covered topics such as industrial zones, infrastructure growth, heritage conservation, and land pooling, all aimed at ensuring a synchronized approach towards effective execution of the Master Plan.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/dda-holds-consultations-on-delhi-master-plan-2047-implementation/134050401?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-209052/134050401.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "In Noida\u2019s PG belt, buildings rise nine floors where two are allowed, cables dangle at arms reach", "para": "Noida villages are experiencing a worrying rise in illegal multi-storey paying guest accommodations, which frequently disregard necessary fire safety measures and emergency exits. Many of these properties flout building codes, raising valid structural safety concerns. Despite this, tenants, mainly students and IT workers, often compromise their safety for lower rents and convenience, perpetuating a cycle of unchecked construction driven by high demand.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/in-noidas-pg-belt-buildings-rise-nine-floors-where-two-are-allowed-cables-dangle-at-arms-reach/134044107?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-214430/134044107.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}]}